1
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,740
Something will work out eventually.

2
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:47,260
Hahahahaha!

3
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without work, come to my place.

4
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

5
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:44,760
You called for me, Chief?

6
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,940
Sit down there.

7
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,160
What is it, anyway?

8
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:54,560
You're aware that convenience store robberies
have been happening in a row recently, right?

9
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:59,960
Yes, and most of the incidents have occurred
at a convenience store called Kameari 24.

10
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:03,240
Convenience stores are a bit of a nuisance,
in my opinion.

11
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:07,440
Their security manuals and
employee training are both immature,

12
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,860
and they're full of openings.

13
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:12,940
I suspect they've become
easy prey for thieves.

14
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:16,480
Well, it's a store that an
ex-salaryman president just started up,

15
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,480
so it's understandable that
it's a local convenience store.

16
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,080
Ryotsu.

17
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:23,120
This is the president in question.

18
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,540
He's an inexperienced
convenience store president.

19
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:31,740
Well, having openings isn't always a bad thing,
you know.

20
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:38,660
When I checked the security videotapes from
the Kameari 24 store over the past few days,

21
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:43,420
I found that a suspicious person had
been caught on camera for a long time.

22
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:46,620
They say thieves scout the place out beforehand,
after all.

23
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:47,500
You.

24
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:48,360
Yes, sir!

25
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:54,220
This is you, Ryotsu.

26
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:58,180
Kind of looks like me, kind of doesn't.

27
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:59,600
This is you.

28
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,220
I think it's me, probably.

29
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,480
Look closely. Fast-forward it, okay?

30
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:10,940
It's been over 30 minutes
and you're still reading.

31
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,640
This is patrol, Chief.

32
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:16,860
You're making excuses and reading manga,
aren't you? Manga!

33
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:20,120
Well, at first glance it looks
like I'm reading manga, right?

34
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:23,500
But actually, it's a stakeout, Chief.

35
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,340
Stakeout.

36
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:28,960
I had a feeling a robber would come today,
so I'm pretending to read manga...

37
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,380
Hey, fast-forward it three hours.

38
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:36,488
Well, I waited, but they didn't really come,

39
00:03:36,538 --> 00:03:38,895
so I thought about heading
back to the police box,

40
00:03:38,945 --> 00:03:40,600
but I'm continuing the stakeout after all!

41
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:44,645
Do you really think I'd
fall for such nonsense?

42
00:03:44,695 --> 00:03:47,200
Slacking off on night duty to read manga,
what's the meaning of this?

43
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,612
It's not standing reading,

44
00:03:50,662 --> 00:03:52,120
it's sitting reading.

45
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:56,380
Idiot! At your age,
aren't you ashamed of yourself?

46
00:03:56,560 --> 00:04:00,560
But I want to read the latest
manga issue before anyone else!

47
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:03,960
A lazy, irresponsible, careless

48
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,920
slacker like you, a useless cop,
has no place on this beat!

49
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:08,820
You're fired, right now!

50
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:10,260
I can't breathe!

51
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,100
Now, now, Ohara-san,

52
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:13,560
that's enough.

53
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:19,340
The lapse in supervising my subordinate
is my responsibility as his superior.

54
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:20,540
No.

55
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:24,880
For that store, it's more reassuring
to have a police officer around.

56
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:27,100
Did you hear that, Chief?

57
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,200
Owner, could you tell us a little more?

58
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:33,359
Of the Kameari 24 stores
in the neighborhood,

59
00:04:33,409 --> 00:04:36,880
only the No. 5 store,
where Mr. Ryotsu frequently stops by,

60
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:39,820
hasn't been robbed yet, so to speak.

61
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:42,980
Ahem! See, did you hear that, Chief?

62
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,985
Even while stopping by to read manga,

63
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:48,380
I was still doing my duty properly.

64
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:51,140
Gah did something just...

65
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:53,200
flash?

66
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:57,520
This is the convenience
store ordering office.

67
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:06,940
So it's a delivery police, is that it?

68
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,880
The 23 wards of Tokyo have the
most expensive land in Japan,

69
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:15,120
so even though the Metropolitan Police wants to add more police boxes,
it simply can't.

70
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,440
This is a map of the
area around the station.

71
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:21,760
The X marks are police boxes,
and the red circles are convenience stores.

72
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:25,240
Ryotsu, state the key points.
The key points.

73
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:27,500
The important part starts here.

74
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:31,700
Meanwhile, convenience stores exposed
to shoplifting and robbery threats

75
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:35,580
badly need security, as you can see.

76
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:40,220
That's why our Katsushika station, ahead
of the whole country, will experimentally

77
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:41,960
introduce the Delivery Police.

78
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:46,200
In other words, we will dispatch police
officers to work at convenience stores.

79
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:46,700
What?

80
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:50,100
Rather than a distant police box,
a convenience store right nearby.

81
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:54,660
If we send officers to convenience stores one by one,
we can start right away.

82
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:59,800
With a police box inside the convenience store right in our neighborhood,
the town's crime prevention will also improve.

83
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:04,440
This is a brilliant idea, like Columbus's egg:
killing two birds with one stone.

84
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,340
Ooh.

85
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:11,120
To start things off, the members of my Kōen-mae police box,
the one I came up with the idea for,

86
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:14,720
will work at convenience stores
and prove how effective it is.

87
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:18,920
Before long, the day when Delivery Police
are commonplace will certainly come.

88
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:23,840
Thanks to Delivery Police,
Japan's myth of safety will be revived.

89
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:33,280
And the name of Chief Tonda, who pioneered that path,
will be passed down for generations to come.

90
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:35,120
M-my name...

91
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,060
Hey,

92
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:37,440
my name...

93
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,760
No, no,

94
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:40,960
will be passed down.

95
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,980
So that's Chief Tonda?

96
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,940
What do you think of this plan?

97
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:47,940
Of course I'm in.

98
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:48,880
Thank you very much.

99
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:53,420
With this, I'll be hanging around
convenience stores 24 hours a day.

100
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,640
This place is too conspicuous.

101
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,240
Move that bookshelf over there right away.

102
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:09,680
Ryotsu

103
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,120
Don't be selfish.

104
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:14,860
Do your best for a bright
21st century, Buchon.

105
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:18,740
Improving the police image is part of the job,
you know.

106
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:21,020
Like a department store reception desk.

107
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:26,360
Be charming to everyone, smile, smile.

108
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:36,060
Can't do that? If you can't even adapt to this much change in the times,
Chief, you'll be next to get the boot, you know what?

109
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:41,980
Good work. You're really good at playing the store president,
aren't you? Right?

110
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:47,940
You fit right in with everyone around you, don't you?
Right? Sabu-cho, sit down, sit down...

111
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:51,200
Come on, Chief, smile, smile!

112
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:55,640
I patrol your store every day, so

113
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:59,940
if there's anything you need,
don't hesitate to tell me.

114
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:02,320
Yes, well, this is part of my duty.

115
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,540
Of course.

116
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:06,020
Well then, Yasuoka, I'm counting on you.

117
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:09,820
Please take good care of things.

118
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:10,820
Yes.

119
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:13,140
Well then, sorry to have bothered you.

120
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:15,040
You're going too?

121
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,320
Good luck.

122
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,020
He's already gone.

123
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:28,400
Good luck, then.

124
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:33,640
I don't think the Chief usually goes to convenience stores,
does he?

125
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,600
Then he must be even more nervous about it.

126
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,720
He was grumbling and complaining, though.

127
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:42,040
As long as we tie him down over there,
we can relax.

128
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:43,640
Relax about what?

129
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:46,120
Did I just say that?

130
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:50,417
Seiko's at store No. 2, Nakagawa's at No. 3,

131
00:08:50,467 --> 00:08:53,500
Terai's at No. 4, and I'm at No. 5.

132
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:57,140
Just us sitting there will deter crime.

133
00:08:57,220 --> 00:09:00,497
And whatever you do, don't go meddling
in the convenience store operations,

134
00:09:00,547 --> 00:09:03,320
and don't ruin this sweet assignment.

135
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:04,680
Sweet assignment?

136
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,520
Did I just say that?

137
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,280
No, I mean...

138
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:12,720
Alright then,

139
00:09:12,770 --> 00:09:17,540
from now on I get to read the newest manga first,
free for all, yay-yay.

140
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,460
and if I get hungry,
piping hot oden right in front of me!

141
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:24,540
Meat buns, bean buns, pizza buns!

142
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:26,960
Coffee, black tea, oolong tea!

143
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:31,260
And on top of that, it's official duty,
so I'm on top of the world!

144
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:34,140
Nice to work with you, Kanbe-chan.

145
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:34,600
Yes.

146
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:35,780
Ow ow!

147
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:39,120
Kanbe-chan, sorry, but could you
give my shoulders a little tap?

148
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,040
Yes.

149
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:44,780
Sorry, sorry, Dietrich.

150
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:54,700
Leaving the dropped items just as they are

151
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:55,520
What's wrong?

152
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:59,100
Your choice of words is
also rather questionable.

153
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:00,140
You

154
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,240
What?

155
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:03,380
Your...

156
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:04,800
Listen, Chief.

157
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:07,800
Interfering with convenience store work is strictly forbidden,
you know.

158
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,660
No, it's nothing.

159
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:11,620
Shall we go on patrol now?

160
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:13,580
It's past eleven o'clock, after all.

161
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,540
Those guys...

162
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:21,020
Listen, Chief,
I'm not meddling in convenience store work.

163
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:25,180
This is a police officer's duty.

164
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:28,720
The fruit liquor looks good too

165
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:31,660
You two are high schoolers, right?

166
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,700
We were just looking, that's all.

167
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:35,680
Come on, come on.

168
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:37,280
Now, let's go home and study.

169
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:40,180
Tuck your shirt into your pants properly.

170
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:45,140
You two are middle schoolers, aren't you?

171
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:47,100
You shouldn't be reading that kind of book.

172
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:50,420
It's past 11 at night.
Won't your parents scold you?

173
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:51,640
My parents don't really care...

174
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:54,020
Yeah, totally fine.

175
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:56,620
Anyway, go home and get to bed quickly.

176
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:58,060
You have school tomorrow too, right?

177
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:58,460
Yes.

178
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:00,840
What a problem.

179
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:06,140
No, no, this won't do.

180
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:09,500
If you put the bread at the bottom,
it'll get crushed, won't it?

181
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:13,540
Put the heavy things on the bottom and the light,
soft things on top.

182
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,920
Right, thank you for waiting.

183
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:16,620
Thanks.

184
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:23,900
Also, you just put the items you dropped
into the bag and handed them to the customer.

185
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:28,860
In cases like that,
shouldn't you replace them with new items?

186
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:29,920
Shut up.

187
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:30,680
What?

188
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,640
It's none of your business.

189
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:35,580
When you speak,
look at the person you're talking to.

190
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,560
Shut up, old man.

191
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:43,140
To someone like you, with no consideration
for others and no real spirit in you,

192
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:45,440
I don't remember being called
"old man" by anyone.

193
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:51,240
What do you think you're doing?

194
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,400
Are you going to quit your
job over something this small?

195
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:55,820
Young people these days

196
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:57,240
whenever something displeases them,

197
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,900
they give up on things so easily.

198
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,620
As long as you keep on like this,

199
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,780
you won't be able to
escape from where you are.

200
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:14,940
What?

201
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,020
Chief

202
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:21,400
Only Mr. Ohara's first store's
sales have dropped sharply.

203
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:23,480
We really can't have this sort of thing.

204
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,720
What, that's ridiculous!

205
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,280
It's true.

206
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:36,380
The Chief's first store's
sales are plummeting.

207
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:37,960
How did it come to this?

208
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:43,060
Mr. Ohara went and removed all the adult magazines
from the front of the store without permission,

209
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:48,600
and he's been restricting entry
for minors under 16 after 10 p.m.

210
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:52,320
And the young night-shift
part-timer quit too.

211
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:54,160
That's obstructing business, you know.

212
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,600
What authority does the Chief
have to do something like that?

213
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:01,960
Maybe the whole idea of putting a police box in
a convenience store was unrealistic from the start.

214
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,740
Wait, look here.

215
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:08,860
Reiko's second store
and Nakagawa's third store

216
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:13,020
are getting more customers who come to see the two of them,
so sales have shot up.

217
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:15,180
Ever since the police box was
set up in the convenience store,

218
00:13:15,180 --> 00:13:17,500
there hasn't been a single
robbery or shoplifting, right?

219
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:19,100
That's certainly true.

220
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:21,060
Leave the Chief to me.

221
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:23,440
Don't rush, don't make a fuss,
take the long view.

222
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:28,180
Natto, spinach ohitashi, and kinpira gobo.

223
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:30,260
You need to eat more vegetables.

224
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:32,320
You must be short on protein, too.

225
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:34,960
Maybe I'll go with this one after all.

226
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:37,740
You can't keep eating sweet stuff like that.

227
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:43,160
If you're going to have a snack,
have nutritious milk or small fish.

228
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:46,280
Make sure you get your calcium.

229
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:47,260
What's with that old man?

230
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:48,440
Gross.

231
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:50,800
Get me this.

232
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,380
Yes.

233
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:52,440
Chief.

234
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:53,960
Ryotsu.

235
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:57,620
Didn't you just lecture
those girls who left?

236
00:13:57,620 --> 00:14:00,240
No, I wouldn't really call it a lecture.

237
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:03,360
The Chief should just
sit here and keep quiet.

238
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:07,940
If the Chief starts lecturing,
customers will just keep running away.

239
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:11,800
But Ryotsu,
what you're doing is too much to overlook.

240
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:15,980
Most customers stop by a convenience
store because they want to relax.

241
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,640
What's the point of preaching
about life to customers like that?

242
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,360
Didn't a part-timer quit, too?

243
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:22,600
But...

244
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,220
That'll be 130 yen.

245
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:26,580
Oh my.

246
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:31,340
Apart from patrolling outside, you can
just sit and read the newspaper like this.

247
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:31,540
Yaaan.

248
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,060
No way it's you, you're too good at this.

249
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,000
Yasuoka-kun.

250
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:38,940
Hello.

251
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:41,840
How have you been? I was worried about you.

252
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:43,460
Thanks for the other day.

253
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:47,220
With the match coming up,
I was planning to quit anyway.

254
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,140
Match?

255
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:49,640
Huh?

256
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:53,240
Isn't this him, by any chance?

257
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:54,180
What?

258
00:14:57,860 --> 00:15:01,800
When Yasuoka was champion,
he got harassed by a drunk.

259
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:04,940
He meant only to shield himself,
but he ended up throwing a punch.

260
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:08,440
In the end, it was ruled self-defense,

261
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:11,540
but since a pro boxer's punch had
been thrown at an ordinary citizen,

262
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:16,000
he was stripped of his
title and disappeared.

263
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:20,600
Yasuoka is returning to the
ring after 1 year and 7 months,

264
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:23,380
and quite a few people question his ability.

265
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:26,280
That's the situation, so, well,

266
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:30,800
I'll pay you later.

267
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:31,180
Yes.

268
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:33,660
Yasuoka-kun.

269
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:42,400
I didn't know you had such circumstances.

270
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:46,740
So I figured this is what
they call a freeter these days.

271
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,160
Freeter?

272
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:48,660
Yeah.

273
00:15:49,060 --> 00:15:50,840
I thought you knew about me.

274
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:51,540
Yeah.

275
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:57,960
As long as you keep that up,
you won't get out of there!

276
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:00,700
I heard that.

277
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:03,496
Right. Energy drink,

278
00:16:03,546 --> 00:16:05,580
don't push yourself too hard.

279
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,660
I can't win if I don't push myself.

280
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:13,580
Thanks. I'm cutting weight right now,
so I'll drink it after weigh-in.

281
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:16,592
Yeah. Well then,

282
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:19,920
good luck. Good luck!

283
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:30,580
Robberies drop, word spreads? Stubborn old man who sells lectures too,
young people flock to the convenience store?

284
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:33,160
What? What? How did it come to this?

285
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,740
I came by the other day
for career counseling,

286
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:43,800
It's you. Didn't you quit your company?

287
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:47,040
Yes, after that I passed the
certified administrative scrivener exam.

288
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:51,820
That's good. But the hard part starts now,
so don't you dare relax.

289
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:52,120
Yes.

290
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:54,080
Well, then.

291
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:55,740
Good luck.

292
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:57,540
Hello.

293
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,180
You two...

294
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:06,060
Is that you two? I didn't recognize you!

295
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:08,220
We just graduated from Kogeru.

296
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:10,140
We'll be college students
starting this spring.

297
00:17:10,140 --> 00:17:12,760
Other than your clothes,
you don't seem to have changed much.

298
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:16,400
At this rate, isn't going to
university just a waste of time?

299
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,060
How rude!

300
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:20,380
Sorry, sorry.

301
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:23,140
Yes, yes.

302
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:24,980
Chief Ohara.

303
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:27,420
Thanks so much for the
other day when I was lost.

304
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:28,920
Well, well.

305
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,180
Taro, say hello.

306
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:31,940
Hello.

307
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:33,520
Hello.

308
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:35,780
This is just a token of our appreciation.

309
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:36,760
No, that won't do.

310
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:39,060
Grandma, I can't accept something like this.

311
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,540
Come on, don't say that.

312
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:44,840
If the Chief's store bounces back,
we'll be safe for now.

313
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:46,020
But then,

314
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:47,500
President?

315
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:49,100
A new problem has come up.

316
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:54,020
Right now, Mr. Ohara's 1st store is in first place,
and Mr. Ryotsu's 5th store is

317
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:57,700
at the bottom, behind even Terai.
Is my store

318
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:01,180
going to be restructured?
Mr. Ryotsu's 5th store will be cut for now.

319
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:04,520
Wait a minute! We'll bounce back soon,
so don't rush into anything!

320
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:10,080
The delivery police was
my idea in the first place,

321
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:12,880
so why does my store have to be cut?

322
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:16,800
Hey, if I just give the convenience
store a little push with my know-how,

323
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:19,700
I'll have sales at the top in no time.

324
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:22,440
No, that won't do.

325
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,680
That's a new product, isn't it?

326
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,880
You can't put it down
at the bottom like that.

327
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,860
Rearrange them higher up.

328
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,700
The appeal of a convenience
store is new products.

329
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:36,300
Repeat customers come in for exactly that.

330
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:38,280
Like this, I make the POP signs myself,

331
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:40,820
and push the new products hard.

332
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:45,440
This way, I set up a paid browsing corner

333
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:50,000
where adult magazines cost 300 yen per hour.

334
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,520
Manga is 100 yen.

335
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:56,880
Let's set up a game corner
and lure in the kids,

336
00:18:56,880 --> 00:19:00,440
and place lyrics kids would
like at their eye level.

337
00:19:01,540 --> 00:19:03,780
Don't just sit there admiring us,

338
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:06,060
come up with some useful ideas for once.

339
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:08,360
Can't you come up with something
like a boxing event or whatever?

340
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:12,860
With all these measures,
sales should go up soon, right?

341
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:15,240
They haven't.

342
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:27,020
Looks like Ryo-san's 5th store has a customer base skewing toward kids.
Kids may be numerous, but they don't spend much, you know.

343
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:30,080
What about the other stores?

344
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:37,740
Ryo-chuuu, our store's brand goods are popular with girls, you know.
Brand goods.

345
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,520
Wait a minute.

346
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:43,680
I'd like to go with one of these two,
if possible.

347
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:45,120
Well then, let's see you guess.

348
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,180
This one...

349
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:50,660
This one's better, I think.

350
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,480
What is that guy doing?

351
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:54,440
Sorry about that.

352
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:57,660
I was just giving a customer
some advice on clothes.

353
00:19:57,660 --> 00:20:00,180
You're doing that kind of thing too?

354
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:03,560
Yes, I gave some mail-order
advice to a student,

355
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,200
and it got a really good reception.

356
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:08,260
The manufacturer came to us
wanting to carry their products.

357
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,620
She's calling you again. See ya.

358
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:12,020
I didn't know that.

359
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:14,940
Reiko's fashion sense is outstanding,
you know.

360
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,620
What about Nakagawa?

361
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:20,220
At my store, female students
make up 90% of our customers.

362
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:23,020
Character goods and plush
toys are selling well.

363
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,780
I think overall,
that adds up to quite a lot of sales.

364
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:27,600
Shut up.

365
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:30,380
Basically, I'm not involved in
convenience store operations.

366
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:33,300
Wasn't the original rule
that we don't interfere?

367
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:35,580
I've been following the
rules diligently, I have.

368
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:37,820
It's only natural that
we fall behind those guys.

369
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:43,600
You've served at the police box,
and you're also cooperating with the store.

370
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:46,460
How about Terai's store?

371
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:50,900
Hello, Ryo-san?

372
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:54,460
Our store hasn't really been
doing anything different,

373
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:58,200
but we're losing even to
stores that do nothing at all.

374
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:01,340
Are you going to quit, Ryo-san?

375
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:05,380
No, please, just give me one more chance.

376
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:06,420
Understood.

377
00:21:07,620 --> 00:21:09,380
The problem isn't the merchandise selection.

378
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:11,960
I've been too indulgent
with the customers until now.

379
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:14,120
The key to sales is lecturing.

380
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:18,140
Modern people who come to convenience
stores want a father's lectures.

381
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:22,340
We'll copy the Chief's approach and
go for the top sales spot in one go!

382
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:23,980
Ouch, that hurt!

383
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:25,080
Wow, that's fast!

384
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:26,460
Well, you see...

385
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:27,320
Hey!

386
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:30,140
What time do you think it is?!

387
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:31,260
It's half past four in the afternoon.

388
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:34,520
I didn't raise you to be like this.

389
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:35,980
You never raised me!

390
00:21:35,980 --> 00:21:37,780
Don't talk back!

391
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:38,940
N-no way!

392
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:41,320
What is this junk food?

393
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:43,420
Your father won't
tolerate wasteful spending!

394
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:44,780
S-sorry.

395
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:46,920
I'm not finished talking yet.

396
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:50,420
You two are growing kids,

397
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:53,480
so you need to eat more nutritious food!

398
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:55,220
Is this dog food?

399
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,280
No being picky!

400
00:21:57,680 --> 00:22:00,540
If dogs can eat it,
there's no reason humans can't.

401
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:01,760
Yes.

402
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:05,600
That'll be 13,260 yen.

403
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,800
All you do is read manga in the
bookstore without buying anything!

404
00:22:09,520 --> 00:22:10,360
Get out!

405
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:11,300
Waaah!

406
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:12,440
You lot!

407
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:15,500
Who do you think is feeding you?!

408
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:17,380
Daddy's angry!

409
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:20,700
Daddy's angry, Daddy's angry!

410
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:21,700
Daddy's angry, Daddy's angry!

411
00:22:21,700 --> 00:22:22,080
Yes?

412
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:23,500
Idiot!

413
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:26,880
You lot are neither my parent nor my child!

414
00:22:27,180 --> 00:22:27,540
You lot are neither my parent nor my child!

415
00:22:27,580 --> 00:22:28,640
Get out!

416
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:36,580
Why am I getting fired too?!

417
00:22:36,620 --> 00:22:37,220
I'm going to die!

418
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:38,300
No way!

419
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:46,220
I see, yes, understood. That idiot...
apparently the fifth store has closed.

420
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:47,060
Ah

421
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:52,560
Hey there, Akimoto.
We've been waiting for you.

422
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:58,940
Well, have a seat. Ah

423
00:22:59,900 --> 00:23:02,740
You bought it Yeah.

424
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:05,000
Please take this. Yes.

425
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:05,580
Yes.

426
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:10,680
Until your injury heals,
you'll have to go without beer.

427
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:11,100
Hmph.

428
00:23:12,380 --> 00:23:13,240
Here's your change.

429
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:14,520
Yeah, thanks.

430
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:17,500
Here, this is your share.

431
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:18,440
Thank you very much.

432
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:21,820
Congratulations, Yasuoka.

433
00:23:21,820 --> 00:23:24,200
Congratulations, Champion!

434
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:26,300
He's not a champion yet, you know.

435
00:23:26,740 --> 00:23:28,280
Well, anyway, I'm just glad.

436
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:29,260
Cheers!

437
00:23:29,260 --> 00:23:29,960
Cheers!

438
00:23:30,920 --> 00:23:33,420
Man, that's good.

439
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:36,500
Thanks for the lecture, Chief Ohara.

440
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:40,540
You're a sly one.

441
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:44,380
Thanks to this convenience store police box,
I got to meet Chief Ohara,

442
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:46,660
and I've been reborn too.

443
00:23:47,380 --> 00:23:50,680
I'm the one who's glad to
meet a young man like you.

444
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:53,400
Oh my, you two are clearly mutually smitten!

445
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:30,700
It's my idea, but noooooooooo!

446
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:34,420
If you'd kept at it,
the moon would've run away.

447
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:38,200
Because right now isn't everything.

448
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:42,680
Don't get too carried away.

449
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:46,400
Even if you cheat a little, too.

450
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:50,560
Sometimes when you're helping someone.

451
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:52,580
Baby, do you know me?

452
00:24:52,620 --> 00:24:56,780
Facing tomorrow with a nice spirit.

453
00:24:57,860 --> 00:25:04,280
Don't get discouraged, just do what
needs doing, with a cute spirit.

454
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:11,620
What's hard to understand
is that desire to show off.

455
00:25:12,700 --> 00:25:17,340
Look at yourself again,
like this, it's fine, right?

456
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:21,860
Na na na na.

457
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:24,980
Nanananananana.

458
00:25:51,940 --> 00:25:54,140
Surely to the camera.

459
00:25:54,140 --> 00:25:59,340
Everyone, come on over to our town!

460
00:26:00,280 --> 00:26:00,960
Thank you.

